WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.840
It is before dawn.

2
00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:04.460
The house is dark and quiet.

3
00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:07.910
A Sikh has already bathed
and covered their head.

4
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:13.070
Now they repeat one word, silently,
in rhythm with the breath.

5
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:19.470
The word is Waheguru, Wonderful Lord:
the name most Sikhs use for God.

6
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.770
Could saying one word, again and
again, really change who you are?

7
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:28.890
In this mission, you'll discover
what Sikhs mean by nam japna,

8
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.090
meditating on God's Name.

9
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.160
Then you'll follow a Sikh's
set prayers through the day,

10
00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.530
from the early hours to bedtime.

11
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.760
Your mission: find out
whether repeating one word,

12
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:42.680
again and again, can change who you are.
